<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39539" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pultārĭus</span></b> ,
			ĭi, m.
		puls; orig. a vessel for pottage; hence, in gen., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A vessel</i> for various uses, e. g. for warm
			drinks, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 53, 54, § 185</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for must,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 42</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for preserving grapes in,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 43, 7</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for coals for fumigation,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 7, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a
			cupping-glass</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 2, 11</span></i>.</div>
